• Implemented and committed locally on `wip/one-repository-2`.

  **Commit:** `556d15c885b846734090d14abd0ce79603c9679e`  
  **Subject:** `one repository: land on lambdaclass/concrete only`

  Nothing was pushed, no git configuration or real remotes were changed, and the working tree is clean.

  ## Per-file summary

  - `scripts/land/train.sh`: lands only on `$REMOTE`/`origin`; removed `LAND_MIRROR`, `--no-mirror`, mirror preflight/pushes/readbacks; `LAND_REPO` defaults to `lambdaclass/concrete`. Owner sign-off and `review_provenance` remain intact.
  - `scripts/push-both.sh`: pushes exactly one remote using `PUSH_REMOTE`, defaulting to `origin`. Kept its name, shared lock, exact-SHA push, readback, and optional bounded CI wait. It is not a duplicate of the train: it remains the manual publisher, while the train performs candidate integration and validation.
  - `scripts/land/acceptance.sh`: clones and monitors only `origin`; its negative GitHub control defaults to `lambdaclass/concrete`.
  - `scripts/land/signoff.sh`: owner sign-off records are now documented as pushed to `origin` only.
  - `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh`: sandbox no longer configures `lambdaclass`; added exact-output and exact-push-log controls for all required one-repository behavior.
  - `.github/workflows/lean_action_ci.yml`: Landing record uses `${{ github.repository }}`.
  - `scripts/oracle/ORACLE.lock`: byte-for-byte identical to `a27fbb842`’s version; points to the lambdaclass release and has no `mirror_url`.
  - `scripts/oracle/build.sh`: rebuilds from the lock’s single `url`.
  - `docs/LANDING.md`: one-repository landing sequence, configuration, and control documentation.
  - `docs/SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS.md`: lambdaclass repository/runner commands and the approved runner-exposure note.
  - `docs/REVIEW.md`: owner sign-off refs go to `origin`.
  - `AGENTS.md`: one repository and origin-only landing rules.
  - `README.md`: CI badge points to lambdaclass/concrete.
  - `.claude/commands/land.md`: origin-only landing instructions.
  - `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md`: publication target is lambdaclass/concrete.
  - `changelog.d/2026-11-08-one-repository.md`: new fragment describing the switch without the superseded guard.

  `docs/decisions.md` and `ROADMAP.md` were not modified.

  ## Controls and exact assertions

  In `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh`:

  - **Default repository** (`:602`): exact whole-line match for  
    `train: (dry-run) would dispatch: $LAND_GH workflow run CI -R lambdaclass/concrete --ref ci/t1 -f base=$BASE`, with no CI ref pushed.
  - **No `lambdaclass` remote required** (`:660`): verifies that remote is absent and exactly matches  
    `train: landed ${HEAD1:0:10} on origin/main. Members (result: CI run 4242 at ${HEAD1:0:10}):`.
  - **Train pushes no second remote** (`:664`): exact push log must be  
    `push origin $HEAD1:refs/heads/main`; origin reaches the train head and `fork` remains at the base.
  - **`push-both.sh` pushes exactly one remote** (`:741`): exact output  
    `push-both: published ${LOCAL:0:8} on pb-ok/main`, exact push log `push pb-ok $LOCAL:main`, with origin and fork unchanged.
  - **Mirror option removed** (`:636`): exact refusal  
    `train: land: unknown option --no-mirror`.

  ## Mutation results

  Each temporary mutation was reverted immediately after its run:

  - Restored concrete2 as the default: `PASS=232 FAIL=1`; the default-repository control failed and printed the concrete2 dispatch.
  - Added a second train push to `fork`: `PASS=230 FAIL=3`; `land push set` failed, including the fork-unchanged assertion.
  - Reintroduced a required `lambdaclass` remote: `PASS=212 FAIL=24`; the intended no-`lambdaclass` control failed with `train: land: mirror remote required`, followed by downstream refusals.
  - Added a second `push-both.sh` push: `PASS=232 FAIL=1`; the single-remote control failed.

  After restoration: `check_landing_script: PASS=233 FAIL=0`.

  ## Deliberately not carried from `a27fbb842`

  - The superseded URL/remote guard: `LAND_REPOSITORIES`, `LAND_CANONICAL_REPO`, all listed guard functions, `require_remote_repo` calls, stale-clone refusals, and guard-specific tests. Server-side protection and the smaller later guard replace that design.
  - All landing-bot files, systemd units, bot checks, and bot documentation deleted on current main.
  - Guard-only changes to `scripts/land/lib.sh`; that file remains unchanged.
  - Old edits to `docs/decisions.md` and `ROADMAP.md`, reserved for the decisions writer.

  ## Verification

  Ran on commit `556d15c885b846734090d14abd0ce79603c9679e`:

  ```sh
  timeout 1500 systemd-run --user --scope -q \
    -p MemoryMax=8G -p TasksMax=1024 bash scripts/checks/run.sh
  ```

